* Three-pole op-amp macromodel (ngspice) -- for STABILITY questions, where the one-pole
* OPAMP1P cannot say anything (it has 90 degrees of phase margin at any gain).
*   aol, gbw : DC gain and gain-bandwidth of the dominant pole (as OPAMP1P)
*   p2, p3   : the two non-dominant poles, Hz
* A decompensated power amplifier such as the LM1875 ("stable for gains of 10 or more")
* is exactly an amplifier whose p2 / p3 sit BELOW its unity-gain frequency.
.subckt OPAMP3P inp inn out PARAMS: aol=31623 gbw=5.5e6 p2=800k p3=2.2e6 rout=0.1
Rin   inp inn 1G
Gm    0 a  inp inn 1m
Rp    a 0  {aol/1m}
Cp    a 0  {1m/(2*3.141592653589793*gbw)}
E2    b1 0 a 0 1
R2    b1 b 1k
C2    b 0  {1/(2*3.141592653589793*1k*p2)}
E3    c1 0 b 0 1
R3    c1 c 1k
C3    c 0  {1/(2*3.141592653589793*1k*p3)}
Eout  o 0  c 0 1
Rout  o out {rout}
.ends OPAMP3P
